module

public import LeanCategories.Lattices.Valued.FoldingRootsAreFoldsCarrier

/-!
# The reflection in a root of the invariant lattice (`#116`)

The residual of #116 is `RootsAreFoldsOfWallsCarrier` — every root of `M^σ` is a wall root up to
sign
and a Weyl translate. The generators of that group are the reflections in the reflective roots, and
this file supplies them for `M^σ`:

* `rootReflection` — the reflection `x ↦ x - 2 (v·x)/(v·v) · v` as an element of
  `OrthogonalGroup (M^σ)`, i.e. a lattice **isometry** of the invariant lattice. It is Mathlib's
  `Module.reflection` along the coroot `IsReflective.coroot`, packaged: no nondegeneracy hypothesis
  is needed, because the coroot is a functional and the reflection is built from it directly.
* `rootReflection_reflective` — the reflection sends reflective roots to reflective roots
  (`IsReflective.reflective_reflection`), which is what makes the Weyl group act on the root set.

Sources: Vinberg, *The groups of unit elements of certain quadratic forms*, Mat. Sb. 87 (1972), §1 —
the reflection `w_α(v) = v - 2(α·v)/(α·α) α` and the group `W(Γ)` generated by reflections in the
roots (the notion #23's `IsChamberWithWalls` is stated for). Mathlib: `LinearMap.IsReflective`
(`LinearAlgebra/RootSystem/OfBilinear.lean:41`), `IsReflective.isOrthogonal_reflection` and
`IsReflective.reflective_reflection` (same file) — the reflection is an orthogonal map of a
symmetric
form, which is the content here.

What this does *not* give: that the reflections *generate* a group acting transitively enough to
realise every root as a wall root up to sign. That is the open item; this file supplies its
generators, not the orbit statement.

## LC-09 record

`rg "Module.reflection|IsReflective.isOrthogonal"` over the repository gives no use — the
repository's
own reflection is `latticeReflection` (`WeylCone.lean`), which is built from a Mathlib `RootPairing`
and requires `IsNondegenerate` plus `IsRegular 2`; the coroot-based `Module.reflection` used here
needs
neither, which is what makes it available for `M^σ`. Nothing ported.

## References

* È. B. Vinberg, Mat. Sb. 87 (1972), §1 (reflections and the group they generate).
* AEGS, arXiv:2312.03638v2, §3.7–3.8 (Lemma 3.4 and its converse, **printed p. 12**).
-/

@[expose] public section

open LeanCategories.Modules.Bilinear.Valued

namespace LeanCategories.Lattices.Valued

variable {L : FiniteProjectiveLatticeCat ℤ ℤ}

/-- **The reflection in a reflective root of the invariant lattice**, as a lattice isometry. No
nondegeneracy hypothesis is needed: the coroot is a functional, and the reflection is built from
it. -/
noncomputable def rootReflection (g : OrthogonalGroup L.obj)
    [Module.Projective ℤ (involutionFixedSubmodule g)]
    (v : (invariantFixedLattice (L := L) g).obj.obj.carrier)
    (hv : IsReflectiveRoot (invariantFixedLattice (L := L) g).obj v) :
    OrthogonalGroup (invariantFixedLattice (L := L) g).obj :=
  ⟨Module.reflection (f := LinearMap.IsReflective.coroot _ hv)
      (LinearMap.IsReflective.coroot_apply_self _ hv), fun x y => by
    have hsymm : ((invariantFixedLattice (L := L) g).obj.obj.bilinMap).IsSymm :=
      LinearMap.IsSymm.mk (fun a b => (invariantFixedLattice (L := L) g).obj.property.2 a b)
    exact LinearMap.IsReflective.isOrthogonal_reflection _ hv hsymm x y⟩

/-- **The reflection sends reflective roots to reflective roots**
(`IsReflective.reflective_reflection`):
the Weyl generators act on the root set of `M^σ`. -/
theorem rootReflection_reflective (g : OrthogonalGroup L.obj)
    [Module.Projective ℤ (involutionFixedSubmodule g)]
    (v : (invariantFixedLattice (L := L) g).obj.obj.carrier)
    (hv : IsReflectiveRoot (invariantFixedLattice (L := L) g).obj v)
    {y : (invariantFixedLattice (L := L) g).obj.obj.carrier}
    (hy : IsReflectiveRoot (invariantFixedLattice (L := L) g).obj y) :
    IsReflectiveRoot (invariantFixedLattice (L := L) g).obj
      ((rootReflection (L := L) g v hv).1 y) := by
  have hsymm : ((invariantFixedLattice (L := L) g).obj.obj.bilinMap).IsSymm :=
    LinearMap.IsSymm.mk (fun a b => (invariantFixedLattice (L := L) g).obj.property.2 a b)
  exact LinearMap.IsReflective.reflective_reflection _ hsymm hv hy

end LeanCategories.Lattices.Valued
